@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Connect your organisation";
}

<h1>Connect your organisation</h1>

<p class="lead"><strong>Who can do this:</strong> a <strong>Global Administrator</strong> or
<strong>Privileged Role Administrator</strong> in your Microsoft Entra tenant. MLCP checks the role
when you sign in; if you were given it a moment ago, sign out and in again.</p>

<h2 class="h5">What we ask for and why</h2>

<partial name="~/Views/Onboarding/_PermissionsTable.cshtml" />

<p>
    We never buy, assign or remove licences with these permissions. You can revoke access at any
    time from <strong>Entra admin centre &rarr; Enterprise applications &rarr; MLCP &rarr;
    Permissions</strong>.
</p>

<h2 class="h5">Steps</h2>
<ol>
    <li>On the connection page, confirm the region your organisation's data will be stored in.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Review permissions and connect</strong>.</li>
    <li>Sign in with your admin account. Multi-factor authentication may be required.</li>
    <li>Review the permissions and click <strong>Accept</strong>.</li>
    <li>You will return to MLCP. Confirming the connection with Microsoft and discovering what your
        agreement makes available usually takes a few minutes.</li>
</ol>

<p class="text-muted">
    <strong>If you are not an administrator:</strong> use <em>Ask my administrator</em> on the
    connection page and we will email them a link explaining the request.
</p>

<a class="btn btn-primary" asp-controller="Onboarding" asp-action="Index">Back to connection status</a>
